Let $p(x) = ax^2 + bx + c.$ Then we have the system of equations
\begin{align*}
4a - 2b + c &= 13, \\
a + b + c &= -2, \\
9a + 3b + c &= 8.
\end{align*}Subtracting the second equation from the first gives $3a - 3b = 15,$ or $a - b = 5.$ Subtracting the second equation from the third gives $8a + 2b = 10,$ or $4a + b = 5.$ Adding these equations gives $5a = 10,$ or $a = 2.$ Substituting this into $a - b = 5$ gives $2 - b = 5,$ or $b = -3.$ Substituting these values into the second equation gives $2 - 3 + c = -2,$ or $c = -3.$ Thus, the polynomial is $p(x) = \boxed{2x^2 - 3x - 3}.$. The answer is \boxed{2x^2-3x-3}
